    {
      "defect": "Resource checks ran before registration and licensing FIFO was not recognized.",
      "change": "Same supplied snapshot classifies consumers before resources. FIFO authorization requires TMP, UID, strict clr-debug-pipe name, current matched owned PID/start/exe/parent and this snapshot's root ancestry. Added only the exact fixed Editor licensing executable; dotnet remains supported. lstat metadata only; contentsRead false."
    },
    {
      "defect": "Transient child details failure aborted discovery without retaining an explicit unresolved identity.",
      "change": "Keep first row identity and first/last error in pending_details, never publish partial owned data. Resolve only in a later supplied snapshot proving absence/zombie or matching identity with complete details. Changed identity remains pending without details adoption. No second ps within discover/snapshot_consumers/monitor. Pending identities block consumer authorization."
    },
    {
      "defect": "Naked closure discovery threw outside monitor and abandoned the bounded cleanup.",
      "change": "Each closure sample catches and records errors, continues the existing natural and TERM-confirmation deadlines, and discovers at most once per supplied snapshot. Skipped/failed samples are not clear. Fresh process/details/ancestry/consumer checks still guard the single TERM opportunity. A successful forced final sample is required for closure_closed; false blocks restore before further process or filesystem access. Original errors remain in monitor evidence and keep run_stage failed."
    }
  ],
